  "title": "Michael DP NDE 7200",
  "date": "1982",
  "content": "My sister and I were resting on a bed when she got up to use the toilet, which was separate from the house. I decided that I would enjoy the breeze from the table fan. The fan was actually in another room connected to a power outlet, also in the other room. It was placed in just behind the window, which separated the two rooms. I got out of the bed and leaned forward, onto the iron bars of the window while I caught the bars with both my hands. I got stuck and screamed for help. I kept screaming but in a short while, I could not scream anymore. I was very distressed and aware that I was dying. Then there was peace, a very strong sense of peace and awareness of death. I started moving upwards and away from my body. I hardly moved a few feet when I saw my sister in the next room, reaching out to switch off the fan. I saw her through an opening, which connected the two rooms, but that view was not possible from where my body was stuck. As soon as she switched off the fan, I was again in my body for maybe 2 seconds before I lost all consciousness. I got up much later and found myself on another bed and my sister was pressing my legs. My whole body was stiff and slowly returning to normal. There was no damage physically and within an hour after waking up, I was able to walk and move with no difficulty.",
